From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 17:50:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS-host: Meyers-singletonize ThreadCreationMutex + Threads
 map
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

arm64ec-mingw doesn't reliably run the global C++ static-ctor chain, so
'std::recursive_mutex ThreadCreationMutex' and 'std::unordered_map<DWORD,...> Threads'
stayed zero-initialized. The first call to ThreadCreationMutex.lock() then
hung in NtWaitForAlertByThreadId because the mutex's internal CS had
DebugInfo=NULL with LockCount in an invalid state — Wine's RtlpWaitForCriticalSection
reported "section ? wait timed out, blocked by 0000".

Wrap both as Meyers singletons (function-local statics) so they construct
on first access regardless of the broken global-ctor chain. Macro aliases
keep the call sites unchanged. Same fix pattern as ConfigLayers in
FEXCore/Source/Interface/Config/Config.cpp.

This unblocks the BTCpuNotifyMapViewOfSection callback in the load_arm64ec_module
init path, which acquires ThreadCreationMutex before HandleImageMap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Madeira-commit: 993d6e1e03b496dd9ef47b057ca9fe9d6c43f4ea
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-fex-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
index 7b04692..e46eebe 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
@@ -149,9 +149,21 @@ std::optional<FEX::Windows::CPUFeatures> CPUFeatures;
 std::optional<FEX::Windows::OvercommitTracker> OvercommitTracker;
 std::optional<FEX::Windows::ImageTracker> ImageTracker;
 
-std::recursive_mutex ThreadCreationMutex;
-// Map of TIDs to their FEX thread state, `ThreadCreationMutex` must be locked when accessing
-std::unordered_map<DWORD, FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState*> Threads;
+// iOS-Mythic: arm64ec-mingw doesn't reliably run global C++ ctors, so the
+// recursive_mutex / unordered_map below would be zero-init'd and any lock()
+// would hang in NtWaitForAlertByThreadId. Wrap as Meyers singletons so they
+// construct on first use regardless of the broken static-init chain.
+inline std::recursive_mutex& GetThreadCreationMutex() {
+  static std::recursive_mutex Mutex;
+  return Mutex;
+}
+#define ThreadCreationMutex GetThreadCreationMutex()
+
+inline std::unordered_map<DWORD, FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState*>& GetThreadsMap() {
+  static std::unordered_map<DWORD, FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState*> Map;
+  return Map;
+}
+#define Threads GetThreadsMap()
 
 std::pair<NTSTATUS, ThreadCPUArea> GetThreadCPUArea(HANDLE Thread) {
   THREAD_BASIC_INFORMATION Info;
